    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0627" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/5–2746: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pinkerton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-05-27T18:00:00+03:00">May 27, 1946—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>170. In reply to request for comments and suggestions on Anglo-American Committee
                    report (reDeptel May 19, 9 a.m.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d474-f1"/>). Arab Higher
                    Committee “reject it completely”. They say Arabs of Palestine are “sole people
                    to decide on their fate and they reject any foreign intervention in their
                    country”. They summarize their demands as (1) abolition of mandate, cessation of
                    Jewish immigration and of land sales; (2) establishment of Arab democratic govt
                    and (3) removal of foreign troops. Full text by air mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pinkerton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
